jkj|n|The act of depositing or deposing; the act of laying down or thrown down; precipitation. ; The act of bringing before the mind; presentation. ; The act of setting aside a sovereign or a public officer; deprivation of authority and dignity; displacement; removal. ; That which is deposited; matter laid or thrown down; sediment; alluvial matter; as, banks are sometimes depositions of alluvial matter. ; An opinion, example, or statement, laid down or asserted; a declaration. ; The act of laying down one's testimony in writing; also, testimony laid or taken down in writing, under oath or affirmation, before some competent officer, and in reply to interrogatories and cross-interrogatories.	a:uj9,126,28;28qg,72,1~uj9,126,28;28qg,72,1	V:1bgy,109,31;1bh1,91,4~1bgy,109,31;1bh1,91,4	n:28qg,82,2;ov4,75,4;16ho,43,8;sem,40,10~sem,40,10;16ho,43,8;ov4,75,4;28qg,82,2	N:1bgy,60,1~1bgy,60,1
